invariant: INV-50
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: the Makefile lists sha512_hw.c beside sha512.c and no
  sha512_avx2.c, so an x86-64 host object with SUITE=aesgcm holds
  sha512_hw.c's five calls and no kernel for them to compress on. A
  relocatable object links with the call undefined, so the object builds,
  and the consumer's link is where it fails, naming a missing symbol and
  not the build that lost its source. The lint reads the packaged source
  list per build, and its host rows with the suite require both files.

--- old
SHA512_HW_SRCS := sha512_hw.c sha512_avx2.c
--- new
SHA512_HW_SRCS := sha512_hw.c
